<h2 id="about">About</h2>
<p>The original version of Minesweeper in Windows XP does not guarantee that every board is solvable, meaning you can end up in a situation where you have to make a random guess to proceed. This implementation aims to generate boards that can be solved using logical deductions alone, inspired by Simon Tatham&rsquo;s implementation of the same idea. While I referred to his excellent <a href="https://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/quasiblog/mines-solver/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreffer ">blog</a> for guidance, the implementation is my own.</p>]]></description></item></channel></rss>